    <md:title>2.7.5: Practice</md:title>
    <md:uuid>93a7c15d-4847-4aee-9e1b-2bc737ac9c6a</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><para>Complete the following questions to practice the skills you have learned in this lesson. </para>
<para>For questions 1 – 8, solve each system of equations to determine if there is one solution, no solution, or infinitely many solutions.</para>

<section class="check-understanding"><exercise data-content-id="2a17b9ee-0868-435e-9a4f-0dbdd1d9ec7c"><problem><para>
      <para> \(\left\{\begin{array}{rcl}5x\;-\;3y\;&amp;=&amp;\;7\\x\;-\;0.6y\;&amp;=&amp;\;1.4\end{array}\right.\) </para>
      </para></problem><solution><para>infinitely many solutions</para><para>
      <para>The correct answer is infinitely many solutions. </para>
    </para></solution></exercise></section></section>
</content>
</document>
